Package: quickunlock
Version: @VERSION@
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: QuickUnlock contributors <noreply@example.com>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-numpy, python3-opencv (>= 4.8), python3-gi,
 gir1.2-gtk-4.0, gir1.2-adw-1 (>= 1.5), libpam-modules, pkexec | policykit-1,
 alsa-utils, systemd
Recommends: gdm3
Homepage: https://github.com/your-name/quickunlock
Description: PIN, face and voice unlock for the GNOME lock screen
 QuickUnlock adds Windows Hello-style sign-in options to Ubuntu: unlock the
 GNOME lock screen with a numeric PIN, face recognition (any webcam, IR
 cameras supported) or voice recognition (experimental).
 .
 Only the GDM login/lock screen is affected; sudo, su, SSH and polkit keep
 requiring the real password. All recognition runs locally on the CPU.
